From: Seeed Studio <techsupport@seeed.cc>
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: board: move VENDOR_SN_MAX/CPUID_LEN out of ROCKCHIP_SET_ETHADDR ifdef

rockchip_set_serialno() (guarded by CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_SET_SN) also uses
VENDOR_SN_MAX/CPUID_LEN, which only build under
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_SET_ETHADDR. Move the shared macros out so the two
features can be configured independently.

diff -urN a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c	2026-09-22 11:06:07.428128657 +0800
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c	2026-09-22 11:06:07.451449508 +0800
@@ -101,7 +101,6 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_SET_ETHADDR
 /*
  * define serialno max length, the max length is 512 Bytes
  * The remaining bytes are used to ensure that the first 512 bytes
@@ -110,6 +109,7 @@
 #define VENDOR_SN_MAX	513
 #define CPUID_LEN	0x10
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_SET_ETHADDR
 #define MAX_ETHERNET	0x2
 
 static int rockchip_set_ethaddr(void)
